&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;India-born Nithya Raman, a relatively little-known Los Angeles City Council member backed by the Democratic Socialists of America (DSA), has defeated incumbent Mayor Karen Bass in a stunning electoral upset, setting the stage for a significant political shift in the country's second-largest city.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Raman's victory represents a generational change in Los Angeles politics, following a similar trend in New York, where democratic socialist Zohran Mamdani was elected mayor last year. However, unlike Mamdani, Raman did not attract widespread national attention during her campaign and sought to establish herself as a candidate willing to differ with her own progressive political camp on certain issues.&lt;/p&gt;
